  "raw_html": "<button type='button' role='link' class='btn btn-link p-0 text-start' id='link_9' aria-label=\" Mukesh versus The State of Madhya Pradesh & Anr pdf\"  class='noToken' href='#' onclick=javascript:open_pdf('9','2024','2024_12_1210_1234','2024INSC1026'); ><font size='4'> <strong>MUKESH<span class='fst-italic'> versus </span>THE STATE OF MADHYA PRADESH & ANR </strong>- <span class='escrText'>[2024] 12 S.C.R. 1210</span><span class='ncDisplay'>2024 INSC 1026</span><input type='hidden' id='cnr' value=ESCR010007602024></button></font><br><strong>Coram : J.B. PARDIWALA<sup style=\"color: #268e97;font-size: 22px;top: 0;\" class=\"tooltip-sup\" data-tooltip=\"Author\">*</sup>, R MAHADEVAN</strong><br> Issue for Consideration Whether the High Court was right in holding that the compromise decree in favor of the appellant needed registration and stamp duty was also required to be paid for mutation of the subject land. Headnotes&dagger; Registration Act, 1908 &ndash; s.17(2)(vi) &ndash; Indian &ndash; Whether the appellant satisfied the conditions enumerated in s.17(2)(vi), 1908 Act and the compromise decree in his favor only asserting his pre-existing rights over the subject land required no registration and was not chargeable with stamp duty: Held: s.17(1), 1908 Act specifies the<br><strong class='caseDetailsTD' ><span style='color:#212F3D' > Decision Date :</span><font color='green'> 19-12-2024</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Case No :</span><font color='green'> CIVIL APPEAL No. 14808/2024</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Disposal Nature :</span><font color='green'> Appeal(s) allowed</font>   <span style='color:#212F3D' > |  Bench :</span><font color='green'> 2 Judges</font></strong><div class='row my-1 mt-2 border bg-light'><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('9','2024','2024_12_1210_1234','2024INSC1026','S')><i <i class='fas fa-columns me-2'></i>Split view</a></div><div class='col-a